<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>

    <!--
      Resolving a string through LocalContext, which is what this app does on
      purpose.

      All sixteen sites lint flags sit in event lambdas: a button's onClick, an
      activity-result callback, a local `fun` called from one of them. None of
      them is in composition, so `stringResource` is simply not callable there,
      it being a @Composable.

      The rule is right in general. Reading a resource during composition through
      LocalContext skips recomposition on a configuration change, and the text
      goes stale. Here the read happens the moment the player presses something,
      so it uses the configuration in force at that moment, which is what an
      error message should say.

      Turned off rather than left at warning level: sixteen findings that are all
      false is noise, and noise is what hides the one that would be real. Worth
      revisiting the day a *composition* site starts reading strings this way,
      because that one would be a genuine bug.
    -->
    <issue id="LocalContextGetResourceValueCall" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      The launcher icon's shape.

      Since logo v3, `ic_launcher_art.png` is a cut-out drawing placed in the
      <foreground> of `ic_launcher.xml`, over a <background> that is a flat
      colour. Neither bitmap fills its square, but they keep the
      `ic_launcher_` prefix, and lint reads any bitmap named that way as a
      legacy icon whose silhouette it judges.

      The reasoning behind the layer split is written where it makes sense, in
      `mipmap-anydpi/ic_launcher.xml`. Nothing to fix here; the rule does not
      describe this case.
    -->
    <issue id="IconLauncherShape" severity="ignore" />

</lint>
